[274.047616, "o", "        \"answer\": \"In adults, lopinavir and ritonavir can be given in a once daily dosing regimen of 800 mg/200 mg (10 mL), or a twice daily dosing regimen of 400 mg/100 mg (5 mL). The once daily regimen is not recommended in pediatric patients, pregnant women, or in combination with certain drugs/mutations. In pregnant patients with no documented resistance substitutions, the recommended dose is 400 mg/100 mg twice daily. In pediatric patients (14 days and older), the dose is calculated based on weight or body surface area (BSA) and should not exceed the adult daily dose of 400 mg/100 mg twice daily.\",\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[274.047708, "o", "        \"citations\": [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
